=Table(columns=[{Factor:"Factor",CBSE",:"Built around NCERT and a structured, concept-based syllabus; it is widely aligned with Indian competitive exams such as JEE, NEET, and CUET.[1][3]",{CISCE:"A broader, content-rich syllabus with strong language depth and separate treatment of subjects such as History/Civics Geography from middle school onward.",{IB:"-based, concept-led, and interdisciplinary with programmes such as MYP and DP designed around global-minded learning.[4]"},{Factor:"Assessment","More exam-led, with longer papers and many question types covering recall, understanding, application, and evaluation.",{CISCECE:"Examheavy but typically descriptive detailed with required external and internal.",{IB:"Uses a mix of internal and external assessment; MYP external is optional and DP adds essays, projects, and other coursework-heavy elements.[7]"}]}],{Factor:"Subject flexibility","Generally more structured with fewer combinations than international curricula.[13]",{CISCE:"Moderate flexibility but still more fixed than IB.",{IB:"Greater flexibility, especially in subject choice and in how learners connect disciplines."}]}
